      "title": "bssgp: Set in_error_pkt",
      "message": "bssgp: Set in_error_pkt\n\nWhenever we receive a BSSGP message indicating an error, set\nin_error_pkt accordingly.  This will prevent higher layer dissectors\nfrom clearing COL_INFO.\n",
      "author_name": "Harald Welte",
      "author_email": "laforge@osmocom.org",
      "authored_date": "2021-02-13T15:45:09.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-02-13T15:46:32.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/5d3834712898179389fe20601d8d64776ef2ca88"
    },
    {
      "id": "318d86852de69427542db92d4a02333a397cac7f",
      "short_id": "318d8685",
      "created_at": "2021-02-13T15:46:32.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "5260be8ab6e3e2eead0b64f42be5e32bc011f58e"
      ],
      "title": "gprs-ns: Mark NS-STATUS as in_error_pkt",
      "message": "gprs-ns: Mark NS-STATUS as in_error_pkt\n\nLike many transport protocols, NS has the ability to include\nthe \"erroneous message\" when reporting errors to its peer in\nNS-STATUS PDUs.\n\nThe current UX however is super annoying:  The BSSGP dissector\nclears COL_INFO and hence if you look at the packet list in wireshark,\nit looks like a valid higher-layer message is transmitted over NS,\nand there is no mention that this is an error (NS-STATUS).\n\nBy simply setting in_error_pkt, the behavior changes: The erroneous\nmessage is still dissected in the protocol details, but COL_INFO\nremains what the NS decoder has to say: NS-STATUS with a decoded\ncause information.\n",
      "author_name": "Harald Welte",
      "author_email": "laforge@osmocom.org",
      "authored_date": "2021-02-13T15:32:52.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-02-13T15:46:32.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/318d86852de69427542db92d4a02333a397cac7f"
    }
